    "id": "fn.ceiling-ieee-1.2-0.1",
    "description": "CEILING(1.2, 0.1) is 1.2 — 15-digit multiple, not IEEE ceil drift to 1.3",
    "tags": ["math", "ceiling"],
    "quirks": ["ieee-vs-excel-precision"],
    "formula": "=CEILING(1.2, 0.1)",
    "expected": { "number": 1.2 },
    "notes": "1.2/0.1 sits slightly above 12 in IEEE; raw ceil would yield 1.3. Excel 15-digit model keeps 1.2. Documented model; live Excel not in CI."
  },
